timestamp: '2026-10-18T16:59:39.132Z'
author: builder
title: 'M1.8 slice 2 round 2: the local runner pin covers the whole tree + node, and only a verified home copy runs'
summary: runner = {node, nodeSha256, dir, treeSha256, entry}, all mandatory; prepareRunner copies the tree into <home>/runners/<treeSha256>/ FIRST and hashes the COPY, verifies node, execs <realpath node> <realpath copied entry>; sessions cannot write the home (session profile), so a swapped source module never reaches a later session
symbols_touched:
  - '#local-runner'
  - ^subscription-only
files_modified:
  - packages/gnomon/src/kernel/local/config.ts
  - packages/gnomon/src/kernel/supervisor/local-session.ts
files_created:
  - packages/gnomon/src/kernel/local/runner-pin.ts
commit: 868ad44f
learnings:
  - Hash the copy
  - 'not the source: that removes the tree TOCTOU entirely'
  - Tree hash = sha256 over sorted rel\0sha lines; symlinks and special files refuse
  - Homebrew node is a 68 KB launcher loading @loader_path/../lib/libnode.dylib so it cannot be copied alone; node is verified then exec'd in place and its dylibs are unpinned (residual; a SEA runner closes it)
tags:
  - decision
  - aegis-h1
body: 'Aegis H1: extraDenyWrite was [] and the pin optional, so a session could rewrite the runner the next local session execs. Now an unpinned runner is an invalid config (no local config, logged).'
